-When `Ctrl+F` opens provider search or YouTube/SoundCloud net search and you're viewing the results list:
+When `Ctrl+F` opens provider search or YouTube/SoundCloud net search and you're viewing the results list, Spotify results identify albums, tracks, and episodes explicitly. A standalone `album` word acts as a natural-language hint, so a query such as `Aja album Steely Dan` ranks album matches first.
 
 | Key | Action |
 |---|---|
 | `↑` `↓` / `j` `k` / `Ctrl+N` `Ctrl+P` | Move cursor (single item) |
 | `Ctrl+U` `Ctrl+D` | Scroll results by page |
 | `Space` | Select or deselect a track for a batch action, then move to the next result |
-| `Enter` | Play the selected track now |
-| `a` | Append all marked tracks to the playlist in result order (or the current track if none are marked) |
-| `q` | Queue all marked tracks to play next in result order (or the current track if none are marked) |
+| `Enter` | Play the selected track now, or load an album and play it from track 1 |
+| `a` | Append all marked results in order; marked albums expand to all their tracks |
+| `q` | Queue all marked results to play next in order; marked albums expand to all their tracks |
 | `p` | (Spotify only) Save the selected track to a Spotify playlist |
 | `Esc` `Backspace` | Back to the search input |
 
